{"id": "EUVD-2026-101712", "enisaUuid": "abd89f73-52d9-3ce0-b0ee-8a320e4df96d", "description": "FreeRDP versions from 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contain a null pointer dereference in the rdpsnd channel when a fragment sets CHANNEL_FLAG_LAST without CHANNEL_FLAG_FIRST. A malicious RDP server can send a malformed rdpsnd PDU on a fresh channel to crash the client and cause denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T15:25:00", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-3mq5-xh88-9v62", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-null-pointer-dereference-via-rdpsnd-fragment"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110829", "GHSA-45cr-5r62-8qcj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a3fdbc6b-00f0-39fb-9893-b7e4533e1238", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dd20f6cf-21af-3506-b74b-db5294f3778b", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}